1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,400
Got new tires this week?

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,000
There's one step most people skip.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,200
Any time a wheel comes off your car,

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,000
the lug nuts can settle over the first few drives.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
As the wheel seats fully against the hub,

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
the clamping force holding it can drop.

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
A nut that felt tight on day one

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
may not read tight on day three.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
One clue is a click or shudder

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
that shows up after new tires — do not guess.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,200
Stop by and we'll take a look

12
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,000
with a torque wrench, set to spec.

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
